From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 04:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(macos): guard null external_begin_frame_source() to stop
 GPU crash under --disable-frame-rate-limit

On macOS, --disable-frame-rate-limit switches the display to a synthetic
begin-frame source, so external_begin_frame_source() returns null. A June 2026
Chromium regression (0348f5809af17d, "viz: Defer UpdateVSyncDisplay and ensure
smooth transition for DisplayLinkMac", crbug 345275139) added an unconditional
virtual call on that pointer in
RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl::DisplayDidReceiveCALayerParams, so the GPU process
dereferences null (EXC_BAD_ACCESS at 0x0 -> exit_code=11) and the window goes
black. Because these patched builds require --disable-frame-rate-limit, every
macOS build on Chromium 150 / 7871 hits this.

Fixed upstream by f0d1fd614eefb (2026-06-18) but NOT backported to the 7871
release branch (present in 7871.46/.47/.48 = all of Electron 43.x), so it must
be applied locally. The guard mirrors the existing display_client_ null-check a
few lines above.

diff --git a/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc b/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
index 0f22973a60c99..25040fa9601d6 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/frame_sinks/root_compositor_frame_sink_impl.cc
@@ -923,7 +923,8 @@ void RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl::DisplayDidReceiveCALayerParams(
   if (display_client_)
     display_client_->OnDisplayReceivedCALayerParams(std::move(ca_layer_params));

-  external_begin_frame_source()->DidReceiveNewCALayerParams();
+  if (auto* ebfs = external_begin_frame_source())
+    ebfs->DidReceiveNewCALayerParams();
 #else
   NOTREACHED();
 #endif
